Step 5. Summarize Logical Relationships  
─────────────────────────────  

The following table summarizes the relationships between the goals and tasks:

• G1 → G2, G3, G4 [FALLBACK( ; , # )]  
  – Justification: The overall mission can be executed either as a sequential single–robot process (G2 and G3) or via multi–robot coordination (G4) when multiple storages are involved.

• G2 → G2.1 and G2.2 [AND sequential]  
  – Justification: The robot must both navigate to and request/retrieve the resource from the storage.

• G2 → G2.3 [Fallback]  
  – Justification: If the battery is low (<10%), the robot must return to recharge and reassign the mission.

• G3 → G3.1 and G3.2 [AND sequential]  
  – Justification: The robot must both navigate to the delivery location and deliver the resource.

• G3 → G3.3 [Fallback]  
  – Justification: If the battery is low (<30%), the robot must return the resource to a checkpoint and reassign the remaining task.

• G4 → AT7 and AT8 [Parallel]  
  – Justification: When multiple storages and destinations are present, collection and delivery tasks are coordinated in parallel.

