─────────────────────────────

- **G1 → G2, G3, G4 [FALLBACK( ; , # )]**  
  *Justification*: The overall mission may be executed sequentially (using a single robot for collection and delivery) or via multi–robot coordination (parallel execution) depending on the number of storages involved.

- **G2 → G2.1 and G2.2 [AND sequential]**  
  *Justification*: Both navigation and resource request/retrieval must be completed in the collection phase.

- **G2 → G2.3 [Fallback]**  
  *Justification*: The battery management branch is activated if the battery level is below 10% during collection.

- **G3 → G3.1 and G3.2 [AND sequential]**  
  *Justification*: Both navigation to the delivery location and the actual delivery must occur in the delivery phase.

- **G3 → G3.3 [Fallback]**  
  *Justification*: The battery management branch is activated if the battery level is below 30% during delivery.

- **G4 → AT7, AT8 [Parallel]**  
  *Justification*: Multi–robot coordination tasks for collection and delivery are executed concurrently to reduce mission time when resources come from different storages.

